---
layout: base.njk
title: Projects
description: WebAssembly tools, runtimes, and protocols built alongside the Zena language.
---

<div class="site-content" id="site-content">
  <div class="projects-index">
    <main class="main">
      <div class="projects-index-container">
        <header class="projects-header">
          <h1 class="projects-title">Projects</h1>
          <div class="projects-intro prose">
            <p>
              Zena targets WebAssembly, so alongside the language we are
              building tools, runtimes, and protocols for workloads where
              WebAssembly shines. Each project solves a concrete need in the
              Zena ecosystem—building code, hosting CLIs, serving packages,
              rendering UI, or running untrusted components—and each benefits
              from being extensible with WebAssembly plugins.
            </p>
            <p>
              These projects follow from two goals. The first is to self-host as
              much of the Zena project as possible: once the compiler compiled
              itself, we kept going—writing the build system, package registry
              and data server, web component layer, and graphical engine in Zena
              as well. The second is to make full use of WebAssembly's
              qualities—capability-based security, portability across hosts, and
              multi-language composition—and show what they make possible. As a
              language that targets only WebAssembly, for Zena to shine and
              succeed, WebAssembly must shine and succeed.
            </p>
            <p>
              Today these tools are written primarily in Zena, paired with
              Wasmtime, Rust, or JavaScript at the host boundary, and they are
              coupled to Zena to varying degrees. Our goal is to decouple them
              from Zena step by step so they are language-agnostic, extensible
              via Wasm components in any language, and useful outside Zena. As
              individual projects mature, some may be renamed and moved into
              standalone repositories to reflect that broader scope.
            </p>
            <div class="custom-block info">
              <p class="custom-block-title">Project maturity</p>
              <p>
                These projects sit at very different stages. Several run every
                day in the Zena monorepo, others are early experiments and
                prototypes, and a few are still design ideas that have not
                started implementation yet. Each project page notes what works
                today and what is still aspirational.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="projects-grid">
          {% for project in projects %}
            <article class="project-card">
              <a
                href="{{ project.link }}"
                class="project-card-link"
                aria-label="{{ project.title }}"
              >
                <div class="project-card-header">
                  <h2 class="project-card-title">{{ project.title }}</h2>
                  <span class="badge {{ project.statusType or 'warning' }}">
                    {{- project.status -}}
                  </span>
                </div>

                <p class="project-card-tagline">{{ project.tagline }}</p>
                <p class="project-card-summary">{{ project.summary }}</p>

                <div class="project-card-footer">
                  <div class="project-card-tags" aria-label="Primary technologies">
                    {% for item in project.stack %}
                      <span class="project-card-tag">{{ item }}</span>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </div>
                  <span class="project-card-cta">
                    Explore <span class="project-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                  </span>
                </div>
              </a>
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</div>
